            <ArticleTitle>Outcomes of coronary artery bypass grafting in patients with a history of illicit drug use.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>593-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To date, no studies have been conducted on the effects of illicit drug use in patients with ischemic heart disease treated with coronary artery bypass grafting. Our retrospective study suggests that current illicit drug use is a significant predictor of cardiovascular complications in the first 6 months after coronary artery bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
